# Line-ending policy.
#
# The GitHub Actions Windows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# rewrites LF -> CRLF in the working tree. That is invisible for source code but
# fatal for the reference-parity suite: several modules pin the SHA-256 of
# `tests/orig_parity/data/02_mpdta_original.csv` so the R/Stata golden numbers
# can never be silently re-locked against a different dataset. Under CRLF
# translation the digest changes and 63 tests error out with "mpdta fixture
# changed" — a checkout artefact reported as a provenance breach.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` keeps every text file byte-identical across platforms, so the
# digests hold everywhere. `text` (rather than `-text`) is deliberate: git still
# treats these as text, so diffs and merges stay readable.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Data fixtures are byte-pinned and/or numerically parsed — never translate.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.dta binary
*.rds binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
